  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Standing On The Moon** (1 review): Reviewer wants to hear Mayer sing this, judging it better suited to him than to Bob [10]\n- **Brown Eyed Women** (1 review): Reviewer says the band ignites this song [7]\n- **Drums and Space** (1 review): Reviewer recalls an instrument in this segment with a very psychedelic tone that stunned them [8]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Drums and Space**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 10 archived performances [12]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2016-07-30.cemc6.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 17 songs; 182 min; rated 5/5 by 3 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer feels the microphones captured the sound pretty well despite the distant lawn spot; Sound quality improves markedly from around Shakedown Street onward [1][9]\n- **deadco2016-07-30.cp4.flac16**: source not stated; 9 songs; 112 min; rated 4/5 by 6 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer attended with a girlfriend seeing her first show; she loved it and became a fan of the band [8]\n- Reviewer stood so far back on the lawn that the band was out of sight; this was the tour closer [9]\n- Bill Walton joined the band on drums [2]\n- Reviewer had seen several Grateful Dead shows, including one of the last, at Shoreline, but this one affected them more [11]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2016-07-30.cemc6.flac16**: taped by John Hermsen; transferred by John Hermsen; source: Peluso CEMC-6 (cards, x-y config) > Sound Devices 722 [1]. Also: Peluso CEMC-6 microphones in x-y configuration into a Sound Devices 722 at 24/96, from center of the lawn [1]\n- **deadco2016-07-30.cp4.flac16**: taped by John Hermsen; transferred by John Hermsen; source: Tascam PE120 bodies with Nakamichi CP-4 Shotgun capsules>Zoom H6 [2]. Also: Reviewer holds a partial first-set recording that picks up near the end of Cassidy; Points to a complete-show transfer of this concert, listed under the cemc6 identifier; This recording is partial, covering only the second set [2][5][7]",
